adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is configured as the empty string (as shown in `.env.example`), an attacker can send the webhook header with an empty value (`""`). Then the comparison becomes `"" !== ""` which is `false`, so the request is accepted.

So the endpoint can be effectively unauthenticated when the secret env var is left empty. (It’s not necessary that *both* env vars are empty; the critical case is the secret being empty.)
